    "result_text": "The full suite is green. There's only one test file in the project (`AcceptanceTest.java`), and it passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` and let everything derived from it rebuild on the new format.\n\n**Core change** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- `nextCustomerCode` now takes `city` and `lastName`. It prepends `CITY3` (upper-cased first three letters of city), keeps `LAST3` (first three of lastName), and computes `NNNN` as a **per-city** 4-digit sequence \u2014 one more than the number of owners already in that city (counted case-insensitively over `findAllOwners()`), replacing the old global owner count.\n- Updated the call site to pass `owner.getCity()`.\n\n**Derived value** \u2014 `Owner.getMembershipNumber()` needed no code change: it prefixes the new `customerCode`, so `<customerCode>-M<YY>` now naturally becomes e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`. The `OwnerMapper` maps these getters into the DTO by name, so the API response reflects the new format automatically.\n\n**Docs/examples** updated for consistency: the javadoc on `nextCustomerCode`, `getMembershipNumber`, and the `openapi.yml` descriptions/examples for `customerCode` and `membershipNumber`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting the regex `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) passes, and `./mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
